IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sg-groups`
IMPORT `sg-interests`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: s 164 -- the register of directors' and chief executive officers' shareholdings.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Part sgb2. Every top-level name begins with the label of its provision.
--
-- HOW IT READS. A company must keep a register showing, for each director, particulars of four kinds of holding (s 164(1)(a) to (d)) and, for each chief
-- executive officer, the same four kinds limited to the company itself (s 164(1A)). The register is filled from the notices the director or officer gives under
-- s 165 (or s 133 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001), within 3 days of receiving each (s 164(5), (6)). Whether the director "has an interest" in a share is
-- s 7's question (sg-interests.l4, purpose `s 7(1) section 164`); for a debenture or participatory interest s 164(14) applies s 7 with subsections (1) and (3) left
-- out. Whether a corporation is a "related corporation" is s 6's (sg-groups.l4), a fact here. Another Act's terms (participatory interest, collective investment
-- scheme) are facts. A duty that is only a "must" with no deadline has no breach path: the regulative rules below say so, and NOTES.md lists them.

§ `Section 164(1) and (1A): the register, and what it must show`

DECLARE `s 164(1) kind of holding` IS ONE OF
    `s 164(1)(a) shares in the company or in a related corporation`
    `s 164(1)(b) debentures of, or participatory interests made available by, the company or a related corporation`
    `s 164(1)(c) rights or options in respect of the acquisition or disposal of shares in the company or a related corporation`
    `s 164(1)(d) contracts under which a person has a right to call for or to make delivery of shares in the company or a related corporation`
    `s 164(1) some other holding`

-- (1): for each director. (2) takes out shares in a related corporation that is a wholly-owned subsidiary of the company or of another corporation.
-- src:13978 | 164.—(1) A company must keep a register showing with respect to
-- src:13979 | each director of the company particulars of —
-- src:13981 | (a) shares in that company or in a related corporation, being
-- src:13982 | shares of which the director is a registered holder or in
-- src:13983 | which he or she has an interest and the nature and extent of
-- src:13984 | that interest;
-- src:13986 | (b) debentures of or participatory interests made available by
-- src:13987 | the company or a related corporation which are held by the
-- src:13988 | director or in which he or she has an interest and the nature
-- src:13989 | and extent of that interest;
-- src:13991 | (c) rights or options of the director or of the director and
-- src:13992 | another person or other persons in respect of the
-- src:13993 | acquisition or disposal of shares in the company or a
-- src:13994 | related corporation; and
-- src:13996 | (d) contracts to which the director is a party or under which he
-- src:13997 | or she is entitled to a benefit, being contracts under which a
-- src:13998 | person has a right to call for or to make delivery of shares
-- src:13999 | in the company or in a related corporation.
@ref s 164(1) (src:13978-13999)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 164(1) kind of holding`
      `the director holds the item, or has the interest, right or benefit the paragraph names` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the item is shares in a related corporation that is a wholly-owned subsidiary of the company or of another corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164(1) the company must show the particulars of the holding in its register of the director's shareholdings` MEANS
    IF kind EQUALS `s 164(1) some other holding`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the subsection lists four kinds of particulars without "only"
    ELSE IF (kind EQUALS `s 164(1)(a) shares in the company or in a related corporation`) AND `the item is shares in a related corporation that is a wholly-owned subsidiary of the company or of another corporation`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company need not show, in its register with respect to a director, particulars of shares in a related corporation that is a wholly‑owned subsidiary of the company or of another corporation" (s 164(2): a flat negative)
         ELSE IF `the director holds the item, or has the interest, right or benefit the paragraph names`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph names holdings "of which the director is a registered holder or in which he or she has an interest" (and the rights, options and contracts it describes); it says nothing of a holding the director has no connection with

DECLARE `s 164(1A) kind of holding` IS ONE OF
    `s 164(1A)(a) shares in the company`
    `s 164(1A)(b) debentures of the company`
    `s 164(1A)(c) rights or options in respect of the acquisition or disposal of shares in the company`
    `s 164(1A)(d) contracts under which a person has a right to call for or to make delivery of shares in the company`
    `s 164(1A) some other holding`

-- src:14003 | (1A) A company must keep a register showing with respect to each
-- src:14004 | chief executive officer of the company particulars of —
-- src:14006 | (a) shares in that company, being shares of which the chief
-- src:14007 | executive officer is their registered holder or in which he or
-- src:14008 | she has an interest and the nature and extent of that interest;
-- src:14010 | (b) debentures of the company which are held by the chief
-- src:14011 | executive officer or in which he or she has an interest and
-- src:14012 | the nature and extent of that interest;
-- src:14014 | (c) rights or options of the chief executive officer or of the
-- src:14015 | chief executive officer and another person or other persons
-- src:14016 | in respect of the acquisition or disposal of shares in the
-- src:14017 | company; and
-- src:14022 | (d) contracts to which the chief executive officer is a party or
-- src:14023 | under which he or she is entitled to a benefit, being
-- src:14024 | contracts under which a person has a right to call for or to
-- src:14025 | make delivery of shares in the company.
@ref s 164(1A) (src:14003-14025)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 164(1A) kind of holding`
      `the chief executive officer holds the item, or has the interest, right or benefit the paragraph names` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164(1A) the company must show the particulars of the holding in its register of the chief executive officer's shareholdings` MEANS
    IF kind EQUALS `s 164(1A) some other holding`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the subsection lists four kinds of particulars without "only"
    ELSE IF `the chief executive officer holds the item, or has the interest, right or benefit the paragraph names`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph names holdings "of which the chief executive officer is their registered holder or in which he or she has an interest" (and the rights, options and contracts it describes); it says nothing of any other

-- The duty as a regulative rule: "A company must keep a register". No time is stated, so a failure cannot reach BREACH (NOTES.md: Rules with no breach path).
DECLARE `s 164 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 164(1) keep the register of the director's shareholdings`
    `s 164(5) enter the particulars in the register`
    `s 164(6) enter the particulars of the change in the register`
    `s 164(8) open the register for inspection`
    `s 164(9) send the copy of the register to the person`
    `s 164(10) send the Registrar a copy of the register`
    `s 164(11) produce the register at the commencement of the annual general meeting`

-- src:13978 | 164.—(1) A company must keep a register showing with respect to
-- src:13979 | each director of the company particulars of —
@ref s 164(1) (src:13978-13979)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 164 act`
`s 164(1) the company must keep a register showing the particulars for each director` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 164(1) keep the register of the director's shareholdings`
    HENCE FULFILLED

§ `Section 164(3) and (4): the wholly-owned subsidiary`

-- (4): "a company is a wholly‑owned subsidiary of another company if none of the members of the firstmentioned company is a person other than" the four heads; the same
-- words as s 5B, so the keel's function answers it (sg-groups.l4), over the members as `s 5B member` records.
-- src:14044 | (4) For the purposes of subsections (2) and (3), a company is a
-- src:14045 | wholly‑owned subsidiary of another company if none of the members
-- src:14046 | of the firstmentioned company is a person other than —
-- src:14048 | (a) the second‑mentioned company;
-- src:14050 | (b) a nominee of the second‑mentioned company;
-- src:14052 | (c) a subsidiary of the second‑mentioned company being a
-- src:14053 | subsidiary none of the members of which is a person other
-- src:14054 | than the second‑mentioned company or a nominee of the
-- src:14055 | second‑mentioned company; or
-- src:14057 | (d) a nominee of such a subsidiary.
@ref s 164(4) (src:14044-14057)
GIVEN members IS A LIST OF `s 5B member`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164(4) the company is a wholly-owned subsidiary of the other company` MEANS
    `s 5B the corporation is a wholly owned subsidiary of the other corporation` members

-- src:14033 | (3) A company that is a wholly‑owned subsidiary of another
-- src:14034 | company is deemed to have complied with this section in relation to a
-- src:14035 | director or chief executive officer of that other company (whether or
-- src:14036 | not he or she is also a director of that company) if the particulars
-- src:14037 | required by this section to be shown in the registers of the
-- src:14038 | firstmentioned company with respect to the director or chief
-- src:14039 | executive officer (as the case may be) are shown in the registers of
-- src:14040 | the second‑mentioned company.
@ref s 164(3) (src:14033-14040)
GIVEN `the company is a wholly-owned subsidiary of another company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director or chief executive officer of that other company (whether or not also a director of the company)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the particulars the section requires for the person are shown in the registers of that other company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164(3) the wholly-owned subsidiary is deemed to have complied with the section for the person` MEANS
    IF    `the company is a wholly-owned subsidiary of another company`
      AND `the person is a director or chief executive officer of that other company (whether or not also a director of the company)`
      AND `the particulars the section requires for the person are shown in the registers of that other company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company that is a wholly‑owned subsidiary of another company is deemed to have complied with this section in relation to a director or chief executive officer of that other company ... if the particulars required by this section ... are shown in the registers of the second‑mentioned company" (a failed "if": marginal reading (a))

§ `Section 164(5) and (6): entering the particulars, within 3 days`

-- The date to be entered for a transaction: the agreement or, if later, the completion; where there was no transaction, the event.
-- src:14080 | (b) the date of —
-- src:14082 | (i) the agreement for the transaction or, if it is later, the
-- src:14083 | completion of the transaction; or
-- src:14085 | (ii) where there was no transaction, the occurrence of the
-- src:14086 | event by reason of which an entry is required to be
-- src:14087 | made under this section.
@ref s 164(5)(b) (src:14080-14087)
GIVEN `there was a transaction by reason of which an entry is required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the agreement for the transaction` IS A DATE
      `the date of the completion of the transaction` IS A DATE
      `the date of the event by reason of which an entry is required` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 164(5)(b) the date the company must enter` MEANS
    IF `there was a transaction by reason of which an entry is required`
    THEN (IF `the date of the completion of the transaction` GREATER THAN `the date of the agreement for the transaction`
          THEN `the date of the completion of the transaction`
          ELSE `the date of the agreement for the transaction`)
    ELSE `the date of the event by reason of which an entry is required`

-- (5)(a): for holdings acquired, or contracts entered into, after the person became a director or chief executive officer, the price or other consideration (if any).
-- src:14071 | relates and in respect of shares, debentures, participatory interests
-- src:14072 | (if applicable), rights or options acquired or contracts entered into
-- src:14073 | after he or she became a director or chief executive officer (as the case
-- src:14074 | may be) —
-- src:14076 | (a) the price or other consideration for the transaction (if any)
-- src:14077 | by reason of which an entry is required to be made under
-- src:14078 | this section; and
@ref s 164(5)(a) (src:14071-14078)
GIVEN `the holding was acquired, or the contract entered into, after the person became a director or chief executive officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a price or other consideration for the transaction by reason of which an entry is required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164(5)(a) the company must enter the price or other consideration` MEANS
    IF `the holding was acquired, or the contract entered into, after the person became a director or chief executive officer` AND `there is a price or other consideration for the transaction by reason of which an entry is required`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the entry of the price or other consideration is required "in respect of shares, debentures, participatory interests (if applicable), rights or options acquired or contracts entered into after he or she became a director or chief executive officer" and "(if any)"

-- (5): the entry is to include "the number and description of shares, debentures, participatory interests (if applicable), rights, options and contracts to which the notice relates".
-- src:14059 | (5) A company must, within 3 days after receiving notice from a
-- src:14060 | director or chief executive officer under section 165(1)(a) of this Act
-- src:14061 | or section 133(1)(a), (b), (c), (d) or (e) of the Securities and Futures
-- src:14062 | Act 2001, enter in its register in relation to the director or chief
-- src:14063 | executive officer (as the case may be) the particulars referred to in
-- src:14064 | subsection (1) or (1A) (as the case may be) including the number and
-- src:14065 | description of shares, debentures, participatory interests
-- src:14066 | (if applicable), rights, options and contracts to which the notice
-- src:14071 | relates and in respect of shares, debentures, participatory interests
-- src:14072 | (if applicable), rights or options acquired or contracts entered into
-- src:14073 | after he or she became a director or chief executive officer (as the case
-- src:14074 | may be) —
@ref s 164(5) (src:14059-14074)
GIVEN `the entry includes the number and description of the shares, debentures, participatory interests (if applicable), rights, options and contracts to which the notice relates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164(5) the entry in the register includes what the subsection requires it to include` MEANS
    IF `the entry includes the number and description of the shares, debentures, participatory interests (if applicable), rights, options and contracts to which the notice relates`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "enter in its register ... the particulars referred to in subsection (1) or (1A) (as the case may be) including the number and description of shares, debentures, participatory interests (if applicable), rights, options and contracts to which the notice relates" (a bare "must" not done: the provision's own question, fork F-164-1)

-- src:14059 | (5) A company must, within 3 days after receiving notice from a
