`s 164(5) the company entered the particulars within 3 days after receiving the notice` MEANS
    IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the company received the notice` `the day the company entered the particulars in its register` 3 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company must, within 3 days after receiving notice from a director or chief executive officer ..., enter in its register ... the particulars" (a duty with a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a); a bare "must" not done, fork F-164-1 in NOTES.md)

-- src:14091 | (6) A company must, within 3 days after receiving a notice from a
