      `the day the company entered the particulars of the change in its register` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164(6) the company entered the particulars of the change within 3 days after receiving the notice` MEANS
    IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the company received the notice` `the day the company entered the particulars of the change in its register` 3 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company must, within 3 days after receiving a notice from a director or chief executive officer ..., enter in its register the particulars of the change referred to in the notice" (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a); fork F-164-1)

-- The two duties as regulative rules. The clock counts days from the day the company receives the notice (day 0); the deadline is inclusive.
-- src:14059 | (5) A company must, within 3 days after receiving notice from a
