§ `Section 164(7): no notice by reason of the register`

-- src:14100 | (7) A company is not, by reason of anything done under this
-- src:14101 | section, to be taken for any purpose to have notice of or to be put upon
-- src:14102 | inquiry as to the right of a person or in relation to a share in debenture
-- src:14103 | of or participatory interest made available by the company.
@ref s 164(7) (src:14100-14103)
GIVEN `the company is said to have notice or to be put upon inquiry by reason only of something done under section 164` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164(7) the company is taken to have notice of, or to be put upon inquiry as to, the right of a person or a share` MEANS
    IF `the company is said to have notice or to be put upon inquiry by reason only of something done under section 164`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company is not, by reason of anything done under this section, to be taken for any purpose to have notice of or to be put upon inquiry as to the right of a person or in relation to a share in debenture of or participatory interest made available by the company" (a flat negative)
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of notice "by reason of anything done under this section" and says nothing of notice from any other source

§ `Section 164(8): where the register is kept, and who may inspect it`

-- src:14105 | (8) A company must, subject to this section, keep its register at the
-- src:14106 | registered office of the company and the register must be open for
-- src:14107 | inspection by a member of the company without charge and by any
-- src:14108 | other person on payment for each inspection of a sum of $3 or such
-- src:14109 | lesser sum as the company requires.
@ref s 164(8) (src:14105-14109)
GIVEN `the company keeps its register at its registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164(8) the company has kept its register at its registered office` MEANS
    IF `the company keeps its register at its registered office`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company must, subject to this section, keep its register at the registered office of the company" (a bare "must" not done: the provision's own question, fork F-164-1)

-- "open for inspection by a member of the company without charge and by any other person on payment for each inspection of a sum of $3 or such lesser sum as the company requires".
-- src:14105 | (8) A company must, subject to this section, keep its register at the
