§ `Section 164(9): a copy of the register`

-- "$1 or such lesser sum as the company requires for every page or part thereof required to be copied": the pages are counted with a part page as a page.
-- src:14111 | (9) A person may request a company to furnish the person with a
-- src:14112 | copy of its register or any part thereof on payment in advance of a
-- src:14113 | sum of $1 or such lesser sum as the company requires for every page
-- src:14114 | or part thereof required to be copied and the company must send the
-- src:14115 | copy to that person within 21 days or such longer period as the
-- src:14120 | Registrar thinks fit after the day on which the request is received by
@ref s 164(9) (src:14111-14120)
GIVEN `the number of pages, counting a part of a page as a page, the person asks to have copied` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 164(9) the most the company may charge in advance for the copy, in Singapore dollars` MEANS
    `the number of pages, counting a part of a page as a page, the person asks to have copied` TIMES 1

-- "within 21 days or such longer period as the Registrar thinks fit after the day on which the request is received".
-- src:14111 | (9) A person may request a company to furnish the person with a
-- src:14112 | copy of its register or any part thereof on payment in advance of a
-- src:14113 | sum of $1 or such lesser sum as the company requires for every page
-- src:14114 | or part thereof required to be copied and the company must send the
-- src:14115 | copy to that person within 21 days or such longer period as the
-- src:14120 | Registrar thinks fit after the day on which the request is received by
@ref s 164(9) (src:14111-14120)
GIVEN `the number of days the Registrar thinks fit, where it is longer than 21 (0 where the Registrar has allowed no longer period)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 164(9) the number of days the company has to send the copy` MEANS
    IF `the number of days the Registrar thinks fit, where it is longer than 21 (0 where the Registrar has allowed no longer period)` GREATER THAN 21
    THEN `the number of days the Registrar thinks fit, where it is longer than 21 (0 where the Registrar has allowed no longer period)`
    ELSE 21

-- src:14111 | (9) A person may request a company to furnish the person with a
-- src:14112 | copy of its register or any part thereof on payment in advance of a
-- src:14113 | sum of $1 or such lesser sum as the company requires for every page
-- src:14114 | or part thereof required to be copied and the company must send the
-- src:14115 | copy to that person within 21 days or such longer period as the
-- src:14120 | Registrar thinks fit after the day on which the request is received by
@ref s 164(9) (src:14111-14120)
GIVEN `the person has requested a copy of the register or any part of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has paid in advance the sum the company requires, which is not more than $1 for every page or part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164(9) the company must send the copy to the person` MEANS
    IF `the person has requested a copy of the register or any part of it` AND `the person has paid in advance the sum the company requires, which is not more than $1 for every page or part`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person may request a company to furnish the person with a copy ... on payment in advance of a sum ... and the company must send the copy" states the duty for a request made on payment in advance and says nothing of a request without it (fork F-164-9 in NOTES.md)

-- src:14111 | (9) A person may request a company to furnish the person with a
-- src:14112 | copy of its register or any part thereof on payment in advance of a
-- src:14113 | sum of $1 or such lesser sum as the company requires for every page
-- src:14114 | or part thereof required to be copied and the company must send the
-- src:14115 | copy to that person within 21 days or such longer period as the
-- src:14120 | Registrar thinks fit after the day on which the request is received by
@ref s 164(9) (src:14111-14120)
GIVEN `the day the company received the request` IS A DATE
      `the number of days the company has to send the copy` IS A NUMBER
      `the day the company sent the copy` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164(9) the company sent the copy in time` MEANS
    IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the company received the request` `the day the company sent the copy` `the number of days the company has to send the copy` Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must send the copy to that person within 21 days or such longer period as the Registrar thinks fit after the day on which the request is received" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))

-- src:14111 | (9) A person may request a company to furnish the person with a
-- src:14112 | copy of its register or any part thereof on payment in advance of a
-- src:14113 | sum of $1 or such lesser sum as the company requires for every page
-- src:14114 | or part thereof required to be copied and the company must send the
-- src:14115 | copy to that person within 21 days or such longer period as the
-- src:14120 | Registrar thinks fit after the day on which the request is received by
@ref s 164(9) (src:14111-14120)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the number of days the company has to send the copy` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 164 act`
`s 164(9) the company must send the copy within the days allowed after the request is received` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 164(9) send the copy of the register to the person`
    WITHIN `the number of days the company has to send the copy`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not send the copy of its register within 21 days, or the longer period the Registrar thought fit, after the day the request was received"

§ `Section 164(10) and (11): the Registrar's notice, and the annual general meeting`

-- src:14123 | (10) The Registrar may by written notice require a company to send
-- src:14124 | to the Registrar within such time as may be specified in the notice a
-- src:14125 | copy of its register or any part thereof.
@ref s 164(10) (src:14123-14125)
GIVEN `the Registrar has given the company written notice requiring it to send a copy of its register or any part of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164(10) the company must send the Registrar a copy of its register` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has given the company written notice requiring it to send a copy of its register or any part of it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Registrar may by written notice require a company to send to the Registrar ... a copy of its register" is the Registrar's power, and the company's duty arises only from a notice given under it

-- src:14123 | (10) The Registrar may by written notice require a company to send
-- src:14124 | to the Registrar within such time as may be specified in the notice a
-- src:14125 | copy of its register or any part thereof.
@ref s 164(10) (src:14123-14125)
GIVEN `the day the company received the Registrar's notice` IS A DATE
      `the number of days the notice specifies` IS A NUMBER
      `the day the company sent the copy to the Registrar` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164(10) the company sent the copy to the Registrar within the time the notice specifies` MEANS
    IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the company received the Registrar's notice` `the day the company sent the copy to the Registrar` `the number of days the notice specifies` Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to send to the Registrar within such time as may be specified in the notice a copy of its register" (a period fixed by the notice the text points to; the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a); the time is an input: fork F-164-10 in NOTES.md)

-- src:14123 | (10) The Registrar may by written notice require a company to send
-- src:14124 | to the Registrar within such time as may be specified in the notice a
-- src:14125 | copy of its register or any part thereof.
@ref s 164(10) (src:14123-14125)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the number of days the notice specifies` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 164 act`
`s 164(10) the company must send the Registrar a copy of its register within the time the notice specifies` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 164(10) send the Registrar a copy of the register`
    WITHIN `the number of days the notice specifies`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not send the Registrar a copy of its register within the time specified in the notice"

-- src:14127 | (11) A company must produce its register at the commencement of
-- src:14128 | each annual general meeting of the company and keep it open and
-- src:14129 | accessible during the meeting to all persons attending the meeting.
@ref s 164(11) (src:14127-14129)
GIVEN `the company produced its register at the commencement of the annual general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company kept the register open and accessible during the meeting to all persons attending` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164(11) the company has complied with the duty to produce its register at each annual general meeting` MEANS
    IF `the company produced its register at the commencement of the annual general meeting` AND `the company kept the register open and accessible during the meeting to all persons attending`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company must produce its register at the commencement of each annual general meeting of the company and keep it open and accessible during the meeting to all persons attending the meeting" (a bare "must" not done: the provision's own question, fork F-164-1)

-- src:14127 | (11) A company must produce its register at the commencement of
-- src:14128 | each annual general meeting of the company and keep it open and
-- src:14129 | accessible during the meeting to all persons attending the meeting.
@ref s 164(11) (src:14127-14129)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 164 act`
`s 164(11) the company must produce its register at the commencement of each annual general meeting` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 164(11) produce the register at the commencement of the annual general meeting`
    HENCE FULFILLED

§ `Section 164(12): the defence`

DECLARE `s 164(12) kind of failure` IS ONE OF
    `s 164(12) a failure to comply with subsection (1)`
    `s 164(12) a failure to comply with subsection (1A)`
    `s 164(12) a failure to comply with subsection (5)`
    `s 164(12) another failure`

-- "It is a defence to a prosecution for failing to comply with subsection (1), (1A) or (5) in respect of particulars relating to a director or chief executive officer if the
-- defendant proves that the failure was due to the failure of the director or chief executive officer to comply with section 165 ... or section 133 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001".
-- src:14131 | (12) It is a defence to a prosecution for failing to comply with
-- src:14132 | subsection (1), (1A) or (5) in respect of particulars relating to a
-- src:14133 | director or chief executive officer if the defendant proves that the
-- src:14134 | failure was due to the failure of the director or chief executive officer
-- src:14135 | to comply with section 165 of this Act, or (as the case may be)
-- src:14136 | section 133 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001 with respect to
-- src:14137 | those particulars.
@ref s 164(12) (src:14131-14137)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 164(12) kind of failure`
      `the defendant proves that the failure was due to the failure of the director or chief executive officer to comply with section 165 of this Act or section 133 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001 with respect to those particulars` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164(12) the section gives the defendant a defence on these facts` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 164(12) another failure` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a defence to a prosecution for failing to comply with subsection (1), (1A) or (5)" limits the defence in its own wording, with no "only", and a prosecution for another failure falls outside the limit (fork F-164-12)
    OTHERWISE
        (IF `the defendant proves that the failure was due to the failure of the director or chief executive officer to comply with section 165 of this Act or section 133 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001 with respect to those particulars`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is a defence ... if the defendant proves that the failure was due to the failure of the director or chief executive officer to comply with section 165 ..." (the ruling of 2026-11-05 on defences: when X is not proved, JUST FALSE for that provision's defence, worded 'this section gives no defence on these facts')

§ `Section 164(13) to (16): terms, interests and deemed holdings`

-- src:14143 | (a) a reference to a participatory interest is a reference to a unit
-- src:14144 | in a collective investment scheme within the meaning of
-- src:14145 | section 2 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001; and
@ref s 164(13)(a) (src:14143-14145)
GIVEN `the thing is a unit in a collective investment scheme within the meaning of section 2 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164(13)(a) the thing is a participatory interest` MEANS
    IF `the thing is a unit in a collective investment scheme within the meaning of section 2 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a reference to a participatory interest is a reference to a unit in a collective investment scheme within the meaning of section 2 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001" (read as a definition that fixes what is meant: fork F-162-12, read the same way)

-- src:14147 | (b) a reference to a person who holds or acquires shares,
-- src:14148 | debentures or participatory interests or an interest in
-- src:14149 | shares, debentures or participatory interests includes a
-- src:14150 | reference to a person who under an option holds or
-- src:14151 | acquires a right to acquire or dispose of a share, debenture
-- src:14152 | or participatory interest or an interest in a share, debenture
-- src:14153 | or participatory interest.
@ref s 164(13)(b) (src:14147-14153)
GIVEN `the person under an option holds or acquires a right to acquire or dispose of a share, debenture or participatory interest or an interest in one` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164(13)(b) the person is a person who holds or acquires shares, debentures or participatory interests or an interest in them` MEANS
    IF `the person under an option holds or acquires a right to acquire or dispose of a share, debenture or participatory interest or an interest in one`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "a reference to a person who holds or acquires shares, debentures or participatory interests or an interest in shares, debentures or participatory interests includes a reference to a person who under an option holds or acquires a right to acquire or dispose of a share"

-- (14): "the provisions of section 7, except subsections (1) and (3) thereof, have effect and in applying those provisions a reference to a share is a reference to a debenture or participatory interest".
-- The keel's `s 7 the person has an interest` applies s 7 without subsection (1)'s purposes; subsection (3) is left out by setting the unit field of the facts FALSE (PLAN.md section 4, seam B).
-- src:14155 | (14) In determining for the purposes of this section whether a
-- src:14156 | person has an interest in a debenture or participatory interest, the
-- src:14157 | provisions of section 7, except subsections (1) and (3) thereof, have
-- src:14158 | effect and in applying those provisions a reference to a share is a
-- src:14159 | reference to a debenture or participatory interest.
@ref s 164(14) (src:14155-14159)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 7 interest facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164(14) the person has an interest in the debenture or participatory interest` MEANS
    IF `s 7 the person has an interest` factsWithoutSubsection3
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the provisions of section 7 "have effect" except subsections (1) and (3): section 7(9) "There is to be disregarded", and for the other limbs a failed "if" or "where" (marginal reading (a))
    WHERE
        factsWithoutSubsection3 MEANS `s 7 interest facts` WITH
            `the person has authority (formal or informal, express or implied) to dispose of, or to exercise control over the disposal of, the shares` IS facts's `the person has authority (formal or informal, express or implied) to dispose of, or to exercise control over the disposal of, the shares`
            `property held in trust consists of or includes the shares and the person has an interest under the trust` IS facts's `property held in trust consists of or includes the shares and the person has an interest under the trust`
            `the person knows, or has reasonable grounds for believing, that the person has that interest under the trust` IS facts's `the person knows, or has reasonable grounds for believing, that the person has that interest under the trust`
            `the person has entered into a contract to purchase a share` IS facts's `the person has entered into a contract to purchase a share`
            `the person has a right, otherwise than by reason of having an interest under a trust, to have a share transferred to the person or to the person's order` IS facts's `the person has a right, otherwise than by reason of having an interest under a trust, to have a share transferred to the person or to the person's order`
            `the person has the right to acquire a share, or an interest in a share, under an option` IS facts's `the person has the right to acquire a share, or an interest in a share, under an option`
            `the person is entitled, otherwise than as a proxy or representative at a meeting, to exercise or control the exercise of a right attached to a share of which the person is not the registered holder` IS facts's `the person is entitled, otherwise than as a proxy or representative at a meeting, to exercise or control the exercise of a right attached to a share of which the person is not the registered holder`
            `the thing is a unit in a collective investment scheme that has been subscribed or purchased on an offer of units, or is issued for such an offer and held by the scheme's manager` IS FALSE
            `the person holds the share as bare trustee` IS facts's `the person holds the share as bare trustee`
            `the person's ordinary business includes the lending of money` IS facts's `the person's ordinary business includes the lending of money`
            `the person holds the interest only by way of security for a transaction entered into in the ordinary course of business in connection with the lending of money` IS facts's `the person holds the interest only by way of security for a transaction entered into in the ordinary course of business in connection with the lending of money`
            `the person holds the interest by reason of holding a prescribed office` IS facts's `the person holds the interest by reason of holding a prescribed office`
            `the interest is a company's interest in its own shares purchased or otherwise acquired in accordance with sections 76B to 76G (including treasury shares)` IS facts's `the interest is a company's interest in its own shares purchased or otherwise acquired in accordance with sections 76B to 76G (including treasury shares)`
            `the interest is a prescribed interest of a prescribed person or class of persons` IS facts's `the interest is a prescribed interest of a prescribed person or class of persons`
            `the bodies corporate through which the person may be deemed to have the interest` IS facts's `the bodies corporate through which the person may be deemed to have the interest`

-- The share case: section 7 with the purpose `s 7(1) section 164`.
-- src:13981 | (a) shares in that company or in a related corporation, being
-- src:13982 | shares of which the director is a registered holder or in
-- src:13983 | which he or she has an interest and the nature and extent of
-- src:13984 | that interest;
@ref s 164(1)(a) (src:13981-13984)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 7 interest facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164(1)(a) the director has an interest in the shares` MEANS
    `s 7 the person has an interest in the shares` `s 7(1) section 164` facts

DECLARE `s 164(15) relationship to the director or chief executive officer` IS ONE OF
    `s 164(15) the wife or husband`
    `s 164(15) a child`
    `s 164(15) another person`

-- (15)(a): a director or chief executive officer is deemed to hold, or to have an interest or a right in or over, shares or debentures if the wife or husband (not herself or himself a
-- director or chief executive officer) holds or has one, or a child under 18 (not himself or herself a director or chief executive officer) holds or has an interest.
-- src:14164 | (15) For the purposes of the application of this section —
-- src:14166 | (a) a director or chief executive officer of a company is
-- src:14167 | deemed to hold or have an interest or a right in or over any
-- src:14168 | shares or debentures if —
-- src:14170 | (i) a wife or husband of the director or chief executive
-- src:14171 | officer (as the case may be) (not being herself or
-- src:14172 | himself a director or chief executive officer thereof)
-- src:14173 | holds or has an interest or a right in or over any
-- src:14174 | shares or debentures; or
-- src:14176 | (ii) a child of less than 18 years of age of that director or
-- src:14177 | chief executive officer (as the case may be) (not
-- src:14178 | being himself or herself a director or chief executive
-- src:14179 | officer) holds or has an interest in shares or
-- src:14180 | debentures; and
@ref s 164(15)(a) (src:14164-14180)
GIVEN relationship IS A `s 164(15) relationship to the director or chief executive officer`
      `the age of the child, in years` IS A NUMBER
      `the wife, husband or child is not themself a director or chief executive officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the wife, husband or child holds, or has an interest or a right in or over, shares or debentures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164(15)(a) the director or chief executive officer is deemed to hold or have an interest or a right in or over the shares or debentures` MEANS
    IF `the wife, husband or child holds, or has an interest or a right in or over, shares or debentures` AND `the wife, husband or child is not themself a director or chief executive officer of the company`
    THEN (CONSIDER relationship
          WHEN `s 164(15) the wife or husband` THEN JUST TRUE
          WHEN `s 164(15) a child` THEN (IF `the age of the child, in years` LESS THAN 18 THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a child of less than 18 years of age of that director or chief executive officer" (a failed "if": marginal reading (a))
          OTHERWISE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is deemed to hold or have an interest or a right ... if (i) a wife or husband ... or (ii) a child of less than 18 years of age" (a failed "if": marginal reading (a))
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(not being herself or himself a director or chief executive officer thereof)" and "holds or has an interest or a right in or over any shares or debentures" are conditions of the deeming "if" (marginal reading (a))

-- src:14182 | (b) any contract, assignment or right of subscription is deemed
-- src:14183 | to have been entered into or exercised or made by, or a
-- src:14184 | grant is deemed as having been made to, the director or
-- src:14185 | chief executive officer (as the case may be) if —
-- src:14187 | (i) the contract, assignment or right of subscription is
-- src:14188 | entered into, exercised or made by, or a grant is made
-- src:14189 | to, the wife or husband of a director or chief
-- src:14190 | executive officer of a company (not being herself
-- src:14191 | or himself a director or chief executive officer
-- src:14192 | thereof); or
-- src:14194 | (ii) the contract, assignment or right of subscription is
-- src:14195 | entered into, exercised or made by, or a grant is made
-- src:14196 | to, a child of less than 18 years of age of a director or
-- src:14197 | chief executive officer of a company (not being
-- src:14198 | himself or herself a director or chief executive officer
-- src:14199 | thereof).
@ref s 164(15)(b) (src:14182-14199)
GIVEN relationship IS A `s 164(15) relationship to the director or chief executive officer`
      `the age of the child, in years` IS A NUMBER
      `the wife, husband or child is not themself a director or chief executive officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract, assignment or right of subscription is entered into, exercised or made by, or a grant is made to, the wife, husband or child` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164(15)(b) the contract, assignment, right of subscription or grant is deemed to have been entered into, exercised or made by, or made to, the director or chief executive officer` MEANS
    IF `the contract, assignment or right of subscription is entered into, exercised or made by, or a grant is made to, the wife, husband or child` AND `the wife, husband or child is not themself a director or chief executive officer of the company`
    THEN (CONSIDER relationship
          WHEN `s 164(15) the wife or husband` THEN JUST TRUE
          WHEN `s 164(15) a child` THEN (IF `the age of the child, in years` LESS THAN 18 THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a child of less than 18 years of age of a director or chief executive officer of a company" (a failed "if": marginal reading (a))
          OTHERWISE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is deemed to have been entered into or exercised or made by ... if (i) ... the wife or husband ...; or (ii) ... a child of less than 18 years of age" (a failed "if": marginal reading (a))
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(not being herself or himself a director or chief executive officer thereof)" is a condition of the deeming "if" (marginal reading (a))

DECLARE `s 164(16) kind of child` IS ONE OF
    `s 164(16) a son or daughter`
    `s 164(16) a stepson`
    `s 164(16) an adopted son`
    `s 164(16) a stepdaughter`
    `s 164(16) an adopted daughter`
    `s 164(16) another relative`

-- src:14203 | (16) In subsection (15), “child” includes stepson, adopted son,
-- src:14204 | stepdaughter and adopted daughter.
@ref s 164(16) (src:14203-14204)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 164(16) kind of child`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164(16) the person is within the word child` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 164(16) another relative` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“child” includes stepson, adopted son, stepdaughter and adopted daughter" does not say that no other relative is a child
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 164(17): the offence`

DECLARE `s 164(17) penalty` HAS
    `s 164(17) the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `s 164(17) the longest imprisonment, in years` IS A NUMBER
    `s 164(17) the further fine for each day the offence continues after conviction, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER

-- src:14211 | (17) If default is made in complying with this section the company
-- src:14212 | and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of
-- src:14213 | an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:14214 | $15,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years and, in
-- src:14215 | the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine of $1,000 for every
-- src:14216 | day during which the offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 164(17) (src:14211-14216)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 164` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164(17) the person is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF (NOT `default is made in complying with section 164`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with this section the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence" (a failed "if": marginal reading (a); split site (i), fork F-164-17 in NOTES.md)
    ELSE IF `the person is the company` OR `the person is an officer of the company who is in default`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the company and every officer of the company who is in default" names who is guilty, with no "only" (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c); split site (i))

-- src:14211 | (17) If default is made in complying with this section the company
-- src:14212 | and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of
-- src:14213 | an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:14214 | $15,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years and, in
-- src:14215 | the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine of $1,000 for every
-- src:14216 | day during which the offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 164(17) (src:14211-14216)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 164` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 164(17) penalty`
`s 164(17) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with section 164` AND (`the person is the company` OR `the person is an officer of the company who is in default`)
    THEN JUST (`s 164(17) penalty` OF 15000, 3, 1000)   -- "a fine not exceeding $15,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine of $1,000 for every day during which the offence continues after conviction"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the penalty is that of "the company and every officer of the company who is in default" where "default is made in complying with this section"

-- src:14211 | (17) If default is made in complying with this section the company
-- src:14212 | and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of
-- src:14213 | an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:14214 | $15,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years and, in
-- src:14215 | the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine of $1,000 for every
-- src:14216 | day during which the offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 164(17) (src:14211-14216)
GIVEN `the number of days the offence continues after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 164(17) the further fine for the days the offence continues after conviction, in Singapore dollars` MEANS
    IF `the number of days the offence continues after conviction` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN 1000 TIMES `the number of days the offence continues after conviction`
    ELSE 0
